window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b>Every living thing is repelled by my corpse-like body...but not my wife.</b><br> <br> Liches are almost gone, only a handful of us left. I must marry to keep my race from extinction, yet how? No living female will ever stoop so low as to marry a lich. People fear us. They say we are the harbingers of death, bad luck, rot, and decomposition.<br> <br> In one last bid to carry out my duty, I request a wife through the Temple. She turns out to be a neglected, sickly thing with trembling hands and downcast eyes, seeking an arranged marriage out of despair.<br> <br> And she's perfect. Her blushes burn hot, her voice rings with feeling, and her kisses taste like summer. She is life personified, all warmth, light, and sweetness, and I crave her like darkness craves the sun.<br> <br> But will she sacrifice her warm, beating heart to a creature of death like me?<br> <br> Contains mature themes.</p>"; 
